  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock id="f-26" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5. None&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantExtensionOrReductionOfTransmissionOrDistributionSystemTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="f-27" contextRef="c-1">&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;6. Refer to Note 8, "Debt and Credit Agreements" of the accompanying "Notes to the Financial Statements" for a discussion of Pepco's debt. The authorizations for the issuances of long-term debt are District of Columbia Public Service Commission (DCPSC) order number 22759 and Maryland Public Service Commission (MDPSC) order number 91810. Pepco has authorizations from FERC to issue short-term debt securities in an amount not to exceed $700 million outstanding at any one time in docket ES25-75-000. The order is effective January 1, 2026 and expires on December 31, 2027.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Pepco periodically issues securities through the private placement markets. Pepco's ability to access the private placement markets will depend on a number of factors at the time of the proposed sale, including other required regulatory approvals, as applicable, current financial condition, securities ratings and market conditions.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
